./tests/binary.rs:3:// This file contains a smattering of tests specifically for checking ripgrep's
./tests/binary.rs:4:// handling of binary files. There's quite a bit of discussion on this in this
./tests/binary.rs:5:// bug report: https://github.com/BurntSushi/ripgrep/issues/306
./tests/binary.rs:6:
./tests/binary.rs:7:// Our haystack is the first 2,133 lines of Gutenberg's copy of "A Study in
./tests/binary.rs:8:// Scarlet," with a NUL byte at line 1870: `abcdef\x00`.
./tests/binary.rs:9://
./tests/binary.rs:10:// The position and size of the haystack is, unfortunately, significant. In
./tests/binary.rs:11:// particular, the NUL byte is specifically inserted at some point *after* the
./tests/binary.rs:12:// first 65,536 bytes, which corresponds to the initial capacity of the buffer
./tests/binary.rs:13:// that ripgrep uses to read files. (grep for DEFAULT_BUFFER_CAPACITY.) The
./tests/binary.rs:14:// position of the NUL byte ensures that we can execute some search on the
